---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Haley Gruensfelder">
  <main class="page-shell about-page-shell">
    <section class="about-page">
      <div class="about-hero">
        <div class="about-copy">
          <p class="section-kicker">About</p>
          <h1>I’m usually trying to figure out what’s getting in the way.</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="about-photo" aria-label="Portrait placeholder"></div>
      </div>

      <p class="about-lead">
        I’m a service designer who likes problems where nobody has the complete picture yet.
      </p>

      <div class="about-intro-block">
        <p>
          I’m naturally curious about how things work—especially the parts most people don’t get to see. I tend to notice the bottlenecks, workarounds, and friction that make a system harder than it needs to be. Then I want to understand why they’re there.
        </p>
        <p>
          At work, I apply that curiosity to products, services, organizations, and the people who rely on them. I use research, systems thinking, frameworks, and strategy to turn ambiguity into something teams can understand and act on.
        </p>
        <p>
          My work is primarily service design, with UX research as an important part of how I approach problems. I enjoy figuring out what we need to learn, designing the right way to learn it, and turning what we discover into a clearer path forward.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-panel-block">
        <div class="about-panel">
          <div class="panel-label">
            <span class="panel-mark">✦</span>
            <span>What I’m good at</span>
          </div>
          <div class="benefits-grid">
            <div class="benefit-item">
              <div class="benefit-head">
                <span class="benefit-icon">◎</span>
                <h3>Seeing the system</h3>
              </div>
              <p>I look beyond individual touchpoints to understand the relationships between people, processes, technology, and incentives that shape an experience.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="benefit-item">
              <div class="benefit-head">
                <span class="benefit-icon">◎</span>
                <h3>Finding the bottleneck</h3>
              </div>
              <p>I like figuring out where a system gets stuck, why it happens, and what might actually change it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="benefit-item">
              <div class="benefit-head">
                <span class="benefit-icon">◎</span>
                <h3>Designing how we learn</h3>
              </div>
              <p>I enjoy creating research methodologies and frameworks for answering questions that don’t come with an obvious playbook.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="benefit-item">
              <div class="benefit-head">
                <span class="benefit-icon">◎</span>
                <h3>Turning complexity into structure</h3>
              </div>
              <p>When there’s a lot of information and no clear way through it, I like creating the models, frameworks, and strategic direction that make the problem easier to navigate.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="benefit-item">
              <div class="benefit-head">
                <span class="benefit-icon">◎</span>
                <h3>Becoming the expert</h3>
              </div>
              <p>Give me a new industry or unfamiliar system and I’ll want to understand how it works, what makes it different, and where the interesting problems are.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="benefit-item">
              <div class="benefit-head">
                <span class="benefit-icon">◎</span>
                <h3>Bringing people along</h3>
              </div>
              <p>I’m a strong speaker and enjoy making complex ideas easier to communicate, helping teams build shared understanding and move toward action.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="about-story-block">
        <h2>A little more about me</h2>
        <p>
          My curiosity doesn’t stop when I leave work.
        </p>
        <p>
          I’m a creative person and a longtime clarinet player. I love board games and video games, particularly anything involving survival, building, or figuring out how a system works. I also have a tendency to watch an unreasonable amount of home improvement and building content.
        </p>
        <p>
          I’m interested in personal finance and enjoy helping the people around me make sense of financial decisions, too. In general, I like learning something well enough that I can turn around and make it easier for someone else to understand.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also care a lot about staying connected to the design community. Since graduating, I’ve stayed involved with Service Design Network Atlanta, where I help create opportunities for designers to practice talking about their work, review portfolios, build confidence, and connect with one another.
        </p>
        <p>
          I benefited from people who were willing to share what they knew when I was starting out. I want to do the same for the people coming up behind me.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-panel-block">
        <div class="about-panel">
          <div class="panel-label">
            <span class="panel-mark">✦</span>
            <span>Career</span>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-list">
            <div class="timeline-item">
              <span class="timeline-year">July 2024 — Present</span>
              <strong>Service Designer — NCR Voyix</strong>
              <p>I work across service design, UX research, strategy, and organizational problems within a product environment. My work has included journey management, research, process improvement, product discovery, benchmarking, and creating frameworks that help teams make better decisions.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="timeline-item">
              <span class="timeline-year">2020 — 2024</span>
              <strong>B.S. Industrial Design — Georgia Institute of Technology</strong>
              <p>I studied Industrial Design with a minor in Technology &amp; Business, building a foundation that combines design practice with business, technology, and systems-oriented problem solving.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="timeline-item">
              <span class="timeline-year">January 2025 — Present</span>
              <strong>Social Chair — Service Design Network Atlanta</strong>
              <p>I help create events and experiences that connect Atlanta’s service design community, including portfolio reviews, elevator-pitch practice, and opportunities for designers to learn, share their work, and get more comfortable putting themselves out there.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="about-panel-block what-i-bring-block">
        <div class="about-panel">
          <div class="panel-label">
            <span class="panel-mark">✦</span>
            <span>What I bring</span>
          </div>
          <div class="bring-list">
            <div class="bring-item">
              <h3>Curiosity with range</h3>
              <p>I’m comfortable entering an unfamiliar industry and getting genuinely interested in how it works.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bring-item">
              <h3>Systems thinking</h3>
              <p>I look beyond individual experiences to understand the larger system shaping them.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bring-item">
              <h3>Research fluency</h3>
              <p>My work spans qualitative and quantitative research, and I’m comfortable figuring out what methodology a problem actually calls for.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bring-item">
              <h3>Strategic structure</h3>
              <p>I enjoy creating frameworks, methodologies, and decision-making tools that turn ambiguity into something actionable.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bring-item">
              <h3>A willingness to go deep</h3>
              <p>Give me a complicated subject and some time to investigate it, and I’ll probably know considerably more about it than I did when we started.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
